    "expert_endorsement_section": {
      "type": "image-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "expert_quote_blk": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p><strong>\"I only had two beers\" is the deadliest phrase on American roads.</strong></p><p>Every year, over 13,000 Americans die in drunk driving crashes. The real tragedy? Almost every driver I pull over genuinely believes they are sober. They trust their \"tolerance\". They drink a cup of black coffee. They wait an hour and feel completely \"fine\". But alcohol is a master of deception. It impairs your judgment long before it impairs your body. You can't feel a 0.08% BAC. You can't guess your exact reaction time. </p><p><strong>The most haunting part isn’t being arrested. It’s when you realize that breath alcohol concentration isn’t just a number; it just cost a life. \"</strong></p>",
            "alignment": "left",
            "mobile_alignment": "mobile-center",
            "text_size": 16,
            "enable_custom_color": false,
            "custom_text_color": "#ff0000",
            "margin_top": 0,
